userStories.description:
**Goal** — Extend canonical rule frontmatter parsing to warn when leading HTML comments displace an otherwise immediately following frontmatter block.

**Motivation** — The old migrator emitted its review notice before the frontmatter, so the whole block — priority included — is dropped without any warning.

**Approach** — Both checks are **deterministic string and list inspections** — no LLM call, no AST parse. The displacement check is a leading-HTML-comment test in the existing parser; the inert check is an emptiness test on the resolved workspace package list. Neither reads file content beyond what the loader already parses.

The displacement check must mirror the existing BOM/blank-line precedent exactly: strip one or more leading HTML comments (and surrounding whitespace) from the front, then require the *remaining* content to start with `---`. It must **not** scan for a `---` occurring anywhere later in the file. Markdown horizontal rules are common in rule bodies — 6 of the 11 files in this repo's own `.nax/rules/` store contain one — so an "is there a `---` somewhere after the comment" test would fire a false warning on every comment-led rule file that happens to use one. A false "your frontmatter is broken" warning is the one outcome this feature must not produce.

**Scope** — In: `parseFrontmatter` warning detection for leading HTML comments and parser tests. Out: lint-level inert-`paths:` warnings and workspace discovery integration (US-002); changing the parse result for comment-displaced frontmatter — the declared `priority`, `paths`, and `appliesTo` remain unhonored, and the file continues to resolve to `FRONTMATTER_PRIORITY_DEFAULT`; detecting frontmatter displaced by leading content other than an HTML comment, a UTF-8 BOM, or blank lines; changing malformed-frontmatter error behaviour.

**Interface**
```typescript
parseFrontmatter(raw: string, filePath: string): ParsedFrontmatter

interface ParsedFrontmatter {
  content: string;
  priority: number;
  paths?: string[];
  appliesTo?: string[];
  stages?: string[];
  warnings: string[];
}
```
